<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<root>
  <!--
    Homespool's shared strings, in the neutral language (English).

    Naming: Area_Thing. A key is never the English text itself - an English-keyed resource means
    changing the wording changes the key, which silently orphans every translation of it.

    Plural keys come in pairs, Thing_One and Thing_Other, and are read through Plural.Format rather
    than by looking one up directly. See Plural.cs for why the pair is the minimum and why more
    forms are a per-language matter.

    Nothing machine-facing belongs here: CSS class names, protocol values, gcode, filenames and
    go2rtc source strings are not text a person reads, and localising one produces a value another
    system rejects. See notes/localisation.md.
  -->
  <xsd:schema id="root" xmlns="" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:msdata="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:xml-msdata">
    <xsd:import namespace="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace" />
    <xsd:element name="root" msdata:IsDataSet="true">
      <xsd:complexType>
        <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
          <xsd:element name="metadata">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" use="required" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="type" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="mimetype" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute ref="xml:space" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="assembly">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:attribute name="alias" type="xsd:string" />
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="data">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
                <xsd:element name="comment" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="2" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" use="required" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
              <xsd:attribute name="type" type="xsd:string" msdata:Ordinal="3" />
              <xsd:attribute name="mimetype" type="xsd:string" msdata:Ordinal="4" />
              <xsd:attribute ref="xml:space" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
          <xsd:element name="resheader">
            <xsd:complexType>
              <xsd:sequence>
                <xsd:element name="value" type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0" msdata:Ordinal="1" />
              </xsd:sequence>
              <xsd:attribute name="name" type="xsd:string" use="required" />
            </xsd:complexType>
          </xsd:element>
        </xsd:choice>
      </xsd:complexType>
    </xsd:element>
  </xsd:schema>
  <resheader name="resmimetype">
    <value>text/microsoft-resx</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="version">
    <value>2.0</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="reader">
    <value>System.Resources.ResXResourceReader, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value>
  </resheader>
  <resheader name="writer">
    <value>System.Resources.ResXResourceWriter, System.Windows.Forms, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b77a5c561934e089</value>
  </resheader>

  <data name="PrinterStatus_Connected" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connected</value>
    <comment>Shown for Undefined and Unknown alike: the printer is talking to us but has not said what it is doing.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Idle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Idle</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Busy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Busy</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Printing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Printing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Paused" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paused</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Finished" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Finished</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Stopped" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stopped</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Error" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Attention" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Waiting for you</value>
    <comment>Firmware means this literally: a dialog is open on the printer and it is blocked until somebody answers - a filament question before a print, load/unload mid-print, crash recovery, nozzle mismatch (printer_state.cpp). Not a synonym for Error, which is something broken rather than something waiting.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Ready" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ready</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrinterStatus_Offline" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Offline</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Printers_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} printer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Printers_Other" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} printers</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Cameras_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} camera</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Cameras_Other" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} cameras</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Files_One" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} file</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Files_Other" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0:N0} files</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Language_Heading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Language</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Language_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The language Homespool uses on the site and in the emails you receive.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Language_FollowBrowser" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use my browser’s language setting</value>
    <comment>The null option. Not the same as choosing English - it follows a person who changes their system language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Language_Save" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Save</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Language_Saved" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Language updated.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Alert_UnhealthySubject" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Homespool is unhealthy</value>
    <comment>Email subject. Sent to administrators, each in their own stored language.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Alert_UnhealthyIntro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Homespool reported a problem:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Alert_UnhealthyFooter" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Printing is unaffected, but recorded history may be incomplete until this is resolved.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Alert_RecoveredSubject" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Homespool has recovered</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Alert_RecoveredBody" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The problems reported earlier have cleared. All health checks are passing again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Account_InvalidUserName" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&apos;{0}&apos; is not a usable username. Use letters, digits, and - . _ only; an email address cannot be a username.</value>
    <comment>Replaces Identity&apos;s own wording, which describes a rule this application does not apply. The three punctuation marks are listed literally and must survive translation.</comment>
  </data>
</root>
